{"id":"single-responsibility","blocks":[{"kind":"prose","id":"the-principle","title":"The Principle","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>A module should have one, and only one, reason to change.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>&quot;Responsibility&quot; here means <em>a reason to change</em>, tied to one stakeholder or concern. A class\nthat formats a report, computes its numbers, and emails it has three reasons to change\n(accounting rules, layout, and delivery), pulled by three different people. SRP says split those\nso each concern lives in its own unit.</p>\n<p>This is the principle the design patterns keep leaning on: Strategy, Facade, and Decorator all\nexist to give one concern one home.</p>\n"},{"kind":"prose","id":"structure","title":"Structure","html":"<figure class=\"structure-diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"851\" height=\"455\" viewBox=\"0 0 851 455\" style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\" class=\"structure-svg\" role=\"img\"><defs><style>@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Handlee&amp;family=Inter:wght@400;700&amp;family=Source+Code+Pro:wght@400;700&amp;family=Caveat:wght@400;700&amp;family=Poppins:wght@400;700&amp;family=Merriweather:wght@400;700&amp;family=Permanent+Marker&amp;family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;700&amp;display=swap');</style></defs><g transform=\"translate(235.5, -96)\"><g opacity=\"1\"><rect x=\"100\" y=\"100\" width=\"180\" height=\"127\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"190\" y=\"126.8\" font-size=\"28\" font-family=\"Handlee, cursive\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">Employee</text><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"153.6\" x2=\"280\" y2=\"153.6\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"224.07999999999998\" x2=\"280\" y2=\"224.07999999999998\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"163.6\" font-size=\"25.2\" font-family=\"Handlee, cursive\" fill=\"#000000\" text-anchor=\"start\" dominant-baseline=\"hanging\">-name</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"193.84\" font-size=\"25.2\" font-family=\"Handlee, cursive\" fill=\"#000000\" text-anchor=\"start\" dominant-baseline=\"hanging\">-salary</text></g><g opacity=\"1\"><rect x=\"-231.5\" y=\"377\" width=\"207\" height=\"120\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"-128\" y=\"403.8\" font-size=\"28\" font-family=\"Handlee, cursive\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">PayCalculator</text><line x1=\"-231.5\" y1=\"430.6\" x2=\"-24.5\" y2=\"430.6\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><line x1=\"-231.5\" y1=\"450.6\" x2=\"-24.5\" y2=\"450.6\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"-221.5\" y=\"460.6\" font-size=\"25.2\" font-family=\"Handlee, cursive\" fill=\"#000000\" text-anchor=\"start\" dominant-baseline=\"hanging\">calculate(emp)</text></g><g opacity=\"1\"><rect x=\"30.5\" y=\"377\" width=\"283\" height=\"120\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"172\" y=\"403.8\" font-size=\"28\" font-family=\"Handlee, cursive\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">EmployeeRepository</text><line x1=\"30.5\" y1=\"430.6\" x2=\"313.5\" y2=\"430.6\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><line x1=\"30.5\" y1=\"450.6\" x2=\"313.5\" y2=\"450.6\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"40.5\" y=\"460.6\" font-size=\"25.2\" font-family=\"Handlee, cursive\" fill=\"#000000\" text-anchor=\"start\" dominant-baseline=\"hanging\">save(emp)</text></g><g opacity=\"1\"><rect x=\"368.5\" y=\"377\" width=\"243\" height=\"120\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"490\" y=\"403.8\" font-size=\"28\" font-family=\"Handlee, cursive\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">ReportFormatter</text><line x1=\"368.5\" y1=\"430.6\" x2=\"611.5\" y2=\"430.6\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><line x1=\"368.5\" y1=\"450.6\" x2=\"611.5\" y2=\"450.6\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"378.5\" y=\"460.6\" font-size=\"25.2\" font-family=\"Handlee, cursive\" fill=\"#000000\" text-anchor=\"start\" dominant-baseline=\"hanging\">format(emp)</text></g><g opacity=\"1\"><path d=\"M 136 227 C 136 324.119, -58.238 279.881, -58.238 377\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><g><path d=\"M-56.978689535178745 376.7615424506366 C-61.43234765395119 367.2597514682697, -66.00672466210618 360.2223535238702, -73.25244448951682 352.0874302915153 M-58.427181151353324 376.6227380875498 C-62.709785079881065 370.3461087793623, -64.65184169813942 364.5786355995292, -72.11513754411837 353.03099162009033\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/></g><g><path d=\"M-56.978689535178745 376.7615424506366 C-52.238476497824934 367.0193252028959, -47.61898234985366 359.9819272584964, -45.252444489516826 352.0874302915153 M-58.427181151353324 376.6227380875498 C-55.86231236822855 370.4103919528191, -50.95689627483439 364.64291877298604, -44.115137544118376 353.03099162009033\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/></g></g><g opacity=\"1\"><path d=\"M 190 227 C 190 302, 175.949 302, 175.949 377\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><g><path d=\"M177.94225344954697 378.4266835562885 C171.4832029301349 368.11609819013455, 169.98430380817987 362.4174631110172, 160.05866573153702 353.51523619208905 M175.24385386294392 377.9802386406809 C170.65000019609735 369.4467969407268, 166.6299128962289 362.0048529542864, 161.54904627388981 353.6743961038855\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/></g><g><path d=\"M177.94225344954697 378.4266835562885 C179.55706313808003 368.2118020478992, 186.13202422407008 362.51316696878183, 188.05866573153702 353.51523619208905 M175.24385386294392 377.9802386406809 C179.7635501401107 369.3896304720022, 184.8570127842556 361.94768648556175, 189.54904627388981 353.6743961038855\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/></g></g><g opacity=\"1\"><path d=\"M 244 227 C 244 317.093, 424.186 286.907, 424.186 377\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><g><path d=\"M423.69338675236276 375.29824871197343 C417.76503753903546 368.5535826067219, 412.3871868548844 359.15560799579356, 408.41806896423867 354.1845868683276 M425.17453634200564 377.8700903635472 C420.7943073191028 372.03301602164555, 418.2070004288386 366.20522435121774, 410.3966001814412 351.86497245233926\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/></g><g><path d=\"M423.69338675236276 375.29824871197343 C428.23815400171316 368.42872066128643, 433.3334197802398 359.0307460503581, 436.41806896423867 354.1845868683276 M425.17453634200564 377.8700903635472 C427.4249470576923 372.1167707261656, 431.4682799060177 366.2889790557378, 438.3966001814412 351.86497245233926\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/></g></g></g><text x=\"425.5\" y=\"436\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Handlee, cursive\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#9aa4b0\">Made with yappydraw.com by Algorisys Technologies</text></svg></figure>"},{"kind":"prose","id":"the-smell","title":"The Smell","html":"<p>One class doing unrelated jobs, so a change to one drags in the others and tests need the world:</p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\"><code class=\"hljs language-\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Report</span> {\n  <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">computeTotals</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\"></span>) { <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* accounting logic */</span> }\n  <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">renderHtml</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\"></span>)    { <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* presentation logic */</span> }\n  <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">sendEmail</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\"></span>)     { <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* delivery logic */</span> }\n  <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">saveToDisk</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\"></span>)    { <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* persistence logic */</span> }\n}\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">// change the email provider → edit the class that also owns accounting math</span></code></pre>"},{"kind":"prose","id":"why-it-matters","title":"Why It Matters","html":"<ul>\n<li>Changes stay local: a layout tweak can&#39;t break the totals.</li>\n<li>Each concern is testable alone, without mocking the others.</li>\n<li>Code is easier to name and find: the class does what its name says.</li>\n</ul>\n"},{"kind":"prose","id":"benefits-and-cautions","title":"Benefits and Cautions","html":"<h3>Benefits</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>High cohesion; low blast radius for changes.</li>\n<li>Small, focused units that are easy to test and reuse.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Cautions</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Taken too far it fragments logic into a hundred one-method classes.</li>\n<li>&quot;One responsibility&quot; is a judgment call. Group by <em>reason to change</em>, not by counting methods.</li>\n</ul>\n"},{"kind":"prose","id":"common-mistakes","title":"Common Mistakes","html":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Confusing &quot;one responsibility&quot; with &quot;one method&quot;</strong>: a class can have several methods that\nall serve one concern.</li>\n<li><strong>Splitting by noun, not by change reason</strong>: the useful axis is who asks for the change.</li>\n<li><strong>Over-fragmenting</strong>: swinging so far that following one feature means opening ten files.</li>\n</ul>\n"},{"kind":"prose","id":"key-takeaways","title":"Key Takeaways","html":"<ul>\n<li>SRP = one reason to change per unit.</li>\n<li>Group code by the stakeholder/concern that drives its change.</li>\n<li>It&#39;s the seed of most patterns: give each concern its own home.</li>\n</ul>\n"},{"kind":"impl","id":"implementations","title":"Implementations","intro_html":"<p>Splitting a <code>Report</code> that computes, renders, and delivers.</p>\n","langs":[{"name":"JavaScript","slug":"javascript","html":"<p><em>Targets modern JavaScript (ES2015+).</em></p>\n<p><strong>❌ Naive</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\"><code class=\"hljs language-js\"><span class=\"hljs-comment\">// Three concerns, three reasons to change, one class.</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Report</span> {\n  <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">constructor</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">data</span>) { <span class=\"hljs-variable language_\">this</span>.<span class=\"hljs-property\">data</span> = data; }\n  <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">computeTotals</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\"></span>) { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-variable language_\">this</span>.<span class=\"hljs-property\">data</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">reduce</span>(<span class=\"hljs-function\">(<span class=\"hljs-params\">a, b</span>) =&gt;</span> a + b, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>); }\n  <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">renderHtml</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\"></span>) { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">`&lt;b&gt;<span class=\"hljs-subst\">${<span class=\"hljs-variable language_\">this</span>.computeTotals()}</span>&lt;/b&gt;`</span>; }\n  <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">send</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">mailer</span>) { mailer.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">send</span>(<span class=\"hljs-variable language_\">this</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">renderHtml</span>()); }\n}</code></pre><p><strong>✅ Idiomatic</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\"><code class=\"hljs language-js\"><span class=\"hljs-comment\">// Each concern owns its change reason.</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">ReportCalculator</span> {\n  <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">totals</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">data</span>) { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> data.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">reduce</span>(<span class=\"hljs-function\">(<span class=\"hljs-params\">a, b</span>) =&gt;</span> a + b, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>); }\n}\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">ReportRenderer</span> {\n  <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">html</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">total</span>) { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">`&lt;b&gt;<span class=\"hljs-subst\">${total}</span>&lt;/b&gt;`</span>; }\n}\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">ReportMailer</span> {\n  <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">constructor</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">mailer</span>) { <span class=\"hljs-variable language_\">this</span>.<span class=\"hljs-property\">mailer</span> = mailer; }\n  <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">send</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">html</span>) { <span class=\"hljs-variable language_\">this</span>.<span class=\"hljs-property\">mailer</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">send</span>(html); }\n}\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">// Composed at the edge:</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">const</span> total = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">new</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">ReportCalculator</span>().<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">totals</span>(data);\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">const</span> html = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">new</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">ReportRenderer</span>().<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">html</span>(total);\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">new</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">ReportMailer</span>(mailer).<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">send</span>(html);</code></pre><p><strong>🧠 Note</strong>: Now an accounting change touches only <code>ReportCalculator</code>, a layout change only\n<code>ReportRenderer</code>. The composition moves to a coordinator (a Facade would be a natural home). The\ncost is more classes; the win is that each changes for exactly one reason.</p>\n"},{"name":"Python","slug":"python","html":"<p><em>Targets Python 3.12.</em></p>\n<p><strong>❌ Naive</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\"><code class=\"hljs language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Report</span>:\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">__init__</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">self, data</span>):\n        <span class=\"hljs-variable language_\">self</span>.data = data\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">compute_totals</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">self</span>):\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>(<span class=\"hljs-variable language_\">self</span>.data)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">render_html</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">self</span>):\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;&lt;b&gt;<span class=\"hljs-subst\">{self.compute_totals()}</span>&lt;/b&gt;&quot;</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">send</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">self, mailer</span>):\n        mailer.send(<span class=\"hljs-variable language_\">self</span>.render_html())</code></pre><p><strong>✅ Idiomatic</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\"><code class=\"hljs language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">ReportCalculator</span>:\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">totals</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">self, data: <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">list</span>[<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>]</span>) -&gt; <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>:\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>(data)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">ReportRenderer</span>:\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">html</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">self, total: <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span></span>) -&gt; <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">str</span>:\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;&lt;b&gt;<span class=\"hljs-subst\">{total}</span>&lt;/b&gt;&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">ReportMailer</span>:\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">__init__</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">self, mailer</span>):\n        <span class=\"hljs-variable language_\">self</span>._mailer = mailer\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">send</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">self, html: <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">str</span></span>) -&gt; <span class=\"hljs-literal\">None</span>:\n        <span class=\"hljs-variable language_\">self</span>._mailer.send(html)\n\ntotal = ReportCalculator().totals(data)\nhtml = ReportRenderer().html(total)\nReportMailer(mailer).send(html)</code></pre><p><strong>🧠 Note</strong>: In Python these can even be plain functions in separate modules\n(<code>calc.py</code>, <code>render.py</code>, <code>deliver.py</code>); the unit of responsibility is the <em>module</em>, not\nnecessarily a class. Either way, each file has one reason to change.</p>\n"},{"name":"Elixir","slug":"elixir","html":"<p><em>Targets Elixir 1.18.</em></p>\n<p><strong>❌ Naive</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\"><code class=\"hljs language-elixir\"><span class=\"hljs-class\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">defmodule</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">Report</span></span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">do</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">compute_totals</span></span>(data), <span class=\"hljs-symbol\">do:</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Enum</span>.sum(data)\n  <span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">render_html</span></span>(data), <span class=\"hljs-symbol\">do:</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&lt;b&gt;<span class=\"hljs-subst\">#{compute_totals(data)}</span>&lt;/b&gt;&quot;</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">send</span></span>(data, mailer), <span class=\"hljs-symbol\">do:</span> mailer.send(render_html(data))\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">end</span></code></pre><p><strong>✅ Idiomatic</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\"><code class=\"hljs language-elixir\"><span class=\"hljs-comment\"># Each concern is its own module.</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-class\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">defmodule</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">Report.Calculator</span></span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">do</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">totals</span></span>(data), <span class=\"hljs-symbol\">do:</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Enum</span>.sum(data)\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-class\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">defmodule</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">Report.Renderer</span></span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">do</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">html</span></span>(total), <span class=\"hljs-symbol\">do:</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&lt;b&gt;<span class=\"hljs-subst\">#{total}</span>&lt;/b&gt;&quot;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-class\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">defmodule</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">Report.Mailer</span></span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">do</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">send</span></span>(html, mailer), <span class=\"hljs-symbol\">do:</span> mailer.send(html)\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\"># Composed in a pipeline:</span>\ndata\n|&gt; <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Report</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Calculator</span>.totals()\n|&gt; <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Report</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Renderer</span>.html()\n|&gt; <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Report</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Mailer</span>.send(mailer)</code></pre><p><strong>🧠 Note</strong>: Elixir&#39;s natural unit of responsibility is the module, and the pipe composes the\nconcerns into a readable flow. Splitting by concern also plays to the language&#39;s strength: each\nmodule is a set of pure functions you can test in isolation.</p>\n"},{"name":"Go","slug":"go","html":"<p><em>Targets Go 1.26.</em></p>\n<p><strong>❌ Naive</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\"><code class=\"hljs language-go\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span> Report <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">struct</span>{ Data []<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> }\n\n<span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">func</span> <span class=\"hljs-params\">(r Report)</span></span> ComputeTotals() <span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> {\n\tsum := <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>\n\t<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> _, n := <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">range</span> r.Data {\n\t\tsum += n\n\t}\n\t<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> sum\n}\n<span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">func</span> <span class=\"hljs-params\">(r Report)</span></span> RenderHTML() <span class=\"hljs-type\">string</span>      { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> fmt.Sprintf(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&lt;b&gt;%d&lt;/b&gt;&quot;</span>, r.ComputeTotals()) }\n<span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">func</span> <span class=\"hljs-params\">(r Report)</span></span> Send(m Mailer) { m.Send(r.RenderHTML()) }</code></pre><p><strong>✅ Idiomatic</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\"><code class=\"hljs language-go\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">package</span> report\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span> Calculator <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">struct</span>{}\n\n<span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">func</span> <span class=\"hljs-params\">(Calculator)</span></span> Totals(data []<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span>) <span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> {\n\tsum := <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>\n\t<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> _, n := <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">range</span> data {\n\t\tsum += n\n\t}\n\t<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> sum\n}\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span> Renderer <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">struct</span>{}\n\n<span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">func</span> <span class=\"hljs-params\">(Renderer)</span></span> HTML(total <span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span>) <span class=\"hljs-type\">string</span> { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> fmt.Sprintf(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&lt;b&gt;%d&lt;/b&gt;&quot;</span>, total) }\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">type</span> Mailer <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">struct</span>{ Client MailClient }\n\n<span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">func</span> <span class=\"hljs-params\">(m Mailer)</span></span> Send(html <span class=\"hljs-type\">string</span>) { m.Client.Send(html) }</code></pre><p><strong>🧠 Note</strong>: Go leans on small packages and types with a tight method set. Separating the three\nconcerns into <code>Calculator</code>, <code>Renderer</code>, and <code>Mailer</code> keeps each type&#39;s method set cohesive, and\na coordinator wires them, so each type now has a single axis of change.</p>\n"},{"name":"Java","slug":"java","html":"<p><em>Targets Java 25.</em></p>\n<p><strong>❌ Naive</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\"><code class=\"hljs language-java\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> java.util.List;\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">// Three concerns, three reasons to change, one class.</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Report</span> {\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">private</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">final</span> List&lt;Integer&gt; data;\n    Report(List&lt;Integer&gt; data) { <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">this</span>.data = data; }\n\n    <span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">computeTotals</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">()</span> { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> data.stream().mapToInt(Integer::intValue).sum(); }\n    String <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">renderHtml</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">()</span> { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&lt;b&gt;%d&lt;/b&gt;&quot;</span>.formatted(computeTotals()); }\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">void</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">send</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(Mailer mailer)</span> { mailer.send(renderHtml()); }\n}\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">// change the email provider → edit the class that also owns accounting math</span></code></pre><p><strong>✅ Idiomatic</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\"><code class=\"hljs language-java\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> java.util.List;\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">// Each concern owns its change reason.</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">ReportCalculator</span> {\n    <span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">totals</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(List&lt;Integer&gt; data)</span> { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> data.stream().mapToInt(Integer::intValue).sum(); }\n}\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">ReportRenderer</span> {\n    String <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">html</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> total)</span> { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&lt;b&gt;%d&lt;/b&gt;&quot;</span>.formatted(total); }\n}\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">interface</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Mailer</span> { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">void</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">send</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(String html)</span>; }\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">ReportMailer</span> {\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">private</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">final</span> Mailer mailer;\n    ReportMailer(Mailer mailer) { <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">this</span>.mailer = mailer; }\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">void</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">send</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(String html)</span> { mailer.send(html); }\n}\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">public</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Demo</span> {\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">public</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">static</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">void</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">main</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(String[] args)</span> {\n        <span class=\"hljs-type\">Mailer</span> <span class=\"hljs-variable\">mailer</span> <span class=\"hljs-operator\">=</span> html -&gt; System.out.println(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;sending: &quot;</span> + html);\n\n        <span class=\"hljs-type\">var</span> <span class=\"hljs-variable\">total</span> <span class=\"hljs-operator\">=</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">new</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">ReportCalculator</span>().totals(List.of(<span class=\"hljs-number\">40</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">35</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">25</span>));\n        <span class=\"hljs-type\">var</span> <span class=\"hljs-variable\">html</span> <span class=\"hljs-operator\">=</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">new</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">ReportRenderer</span>().html(total);\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">new</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">ReportMailer</span>(mailer).send(html); <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// sending: &lt;b&gt;100&lt;/b&gt;</span>\n    }\n}</code></pre><p><strong>🧠 Note</strong>: Java&#39;s unit of responsibility is the class, and at scale the package; in a real\ncodebase these three land in <code>report.calc</code>, <code>report.render</code>, <code>report.deliver</code>. The stateless\n<code>ReportCalculator</code> and <code>ReportRenderer</code> could just as well be static methods; the boundary\nmatters, not the ceremony. And because <code>Mailer</code> is a single-method interface, delivery is\nfaked in tests with a lambda; the split is exactly what made that test cheap.</p>\n"},{"name":"CSharp","slug":"csharp","html":"<p><em>Targets C# 14 / .NET 10.</em></p>\n<p><strong>❌ Naive</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\"><code class=\"hljs language-csharp\"><span class=\"hljs-comment\">// Three concerns, three reasons to change, one class.</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">public</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">sealed</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">Report</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">List&lt;<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>&gt; data</span>)</span>\n{\n    <span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">public</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">ComputeTotals</span>()</span> =&gt; data.Sum();\n    <span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">public</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">string</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">RenderHtml</span>()</span> =&gt; <span class=\"hljs-string\">$&quot;&lt;b&gt;<span class=\"hljs-subst\">{ComputeTotals()}</span>&lt;/b&gt;&quot;</span>;\n    <span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">public</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">void</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">Send</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">IMailer mailer</span>)</span> =&gt; mailer.Send(RenderHtml());\n}\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">// change the email provider → edit the class that also owns accounting math</span></code></pre><p><strong>✅ Idiomatic</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\"><code class=\"hljs language-csharp\"><span class=\"hljs-comment\">// Composed at the edge: top-level statements first, types after.</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span> total = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">new</span> ReportCalculator().Totals(data);\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">var</span> html = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">new</span> ReportRenderer().Html(total);\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">new</span> ReportMailer(mailer).Send(html);\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">public</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">sealed</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">ReportCalculator</span>\n{\n    <span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">public</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">Totals</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">IEnumerable&lt;<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>&gt; data</span>)</span> =&gt; data.Sum();\n}\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">public</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">sealed</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">ReportRenderer</span>\n{\n    <span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">public</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">string</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">Html</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\"><span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span> total</span>)</span> =&gt; <span class=\"hljs-string\">$&quot;&lt;b&gt;<span class=\"hljs-subst\">{total}</span>&lt;/b&gt;&quot;</span>;\n}\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">// Primary constructor: delivery owns its dependency, nothing else.</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">public</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">sealed</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">ReportMailer</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">IMailer mailer</span>)</span>\n{\n    <span class=\"hljs-function\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">public</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">void</span> <span class=\"hljs-title\">Send</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\"><span class=\"hljs-built_in\">string</span> html</span>)</span> =&gt; mailer.Send(html);\n}</code></pre><p><strong>🧠 Note</strong>: Each sealed class is now one expression-bodied member serving one stakeholder;\nan email-provider change touches only <code>ReportMailer</code>&#39;s constructor dependency. In a real\ncodebase the split usually goes further (separate namespaces or projects per concern), and\nthe stateless <code>Calculator</code> and <code>Renderer</code> could just as well be static methods. The unit of\nresponsibility matters more than whether it&#39;s a class.</p>\n"},{"name":"Rust","slug":"rust","html":"<p><em>Targets Rust 1.95 (2024 edition).</em></p>\n<p><strong>❌ Naive</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\"><code class=\"hljs language-rust\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">struct</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Report</span> {\n    data: <span class=\"hljs-type\">Vec</span>&lt;<span class=\"hljs-type\">i32</span>&gt;,\n}\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">impl</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Report</span> {\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">fn</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">compute_totals</span>(&amp;<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">self</span>) <span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">i32</span> {\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">self</span>.data.<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">iter</span>().<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">sum</span>()\n    }\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">fn</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">render_html</span>(&amp;<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">self</span>) <span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">String</span> {\n        <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">format!</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&lt;b&gt;{}&lt;/b&gt;&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">self</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">compute_totals</span>())\n    }\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">fn</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">send</span>(&amp;<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">self</span>, mailer: &amp;Mailer) {\n        mailer.<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">send</span>(&amp;<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">self</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">render_html</span>());\n    }\n}\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">// change the email provider → edit the impl that also owns accounting math</span></code></pre><p><strong>✅ Idiomatic</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\"><code class=\"hljs language-rust\"><span class=\"hljs-comment\">// Each concern is its own module of plain functions: in a real</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">// project: calc.rs, render.rs, deliver.rs.</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">mod</span> calc {\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">pub</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">fn</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">totals</span>(data: &amp;[<span class=\"hljs-type\">i32</span>]) <span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">i32</span> {\n        data.<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">iter</span>().<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">sum</span>()\n    }\n}\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">mod</span> render {\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">pub</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">fn</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">html</span>(total: <span class=\"hljs-type\">i32</span>) <span class=\"hljs-punctuation\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">String</span> {\n        <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">format!</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&lt;b&gt;{total}&lt;/b&gt;&quot;</span>)\n    }\n}\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">mod</span> deliver {\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">pub</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">struct</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Mailer</span>; <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// holds the mail client in real code</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">impl</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Mailer</span> {\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">pub</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">fn</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">send</span>(&amp;<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">self</span>, html: &amp;<span class=\"hljs-type\">str</span>) {\n            <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">println!</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;sending: {html}&quot;</span>);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">fn</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">main</span>() {\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">let</span> <span class=\"hljs-variable\">data</span> = [<span class=\"hljs-number\">40</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">35</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">25</span>];\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">let</span> <span class=\"hljs-variable\">total</span> = calc::<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">totals</span>(&amp;data);\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">let</span> <span class=\"hljs-variable\">html</span> = render::<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">html</span>(total);\n    deliver::Mailer.<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">send</span>(&amp;html); <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// sending: &lt;b&gt;100&lt;/b&gt;</span>\n}</code></pre><p><strong>🧠 Note</strong>: Rust&#39;s unit of responsibility is the module (and at scale, the crate), and functions\ndon&#39;t need a struct to live on, so two of the three concerns are just free functions. The split\nalso plays well with the borrow checker: data flows one direction through small pure pieces\ninstead of every concern borrowing from one shared <code>self</code>.</p>\n"},{"name":"Zig","slug":"zig","html":"<p><em>Targets Zig 0.17-dev.</em></p>\n<p><strong>❌ Naive</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\"><code class=\"hljs language-zig\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">const</span> std = @<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">import</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;std&quot;</span>);\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">// Three concerns in one struct: accounting, layout, delivery.</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">const</span> Report = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    data: []<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">i32</span>,\n\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">fn</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">computeTotals</span>(<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">self</span>: Report) <span class=\"hljs-type\">i32</span> {\n        var sum: <span class=\"hljs-type\">i32</span> = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>;\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">self</span>.data) |n| sum += n;\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> sum;\n    }\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">fn</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">renderHtml</span>(<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">self</span>: Report, buf: []<span class=\"hljs-type\">u8</span>) ![]<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">u8</span> {\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> std.fmt.<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">bufPrint</span>(buf, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&lt;b&gt;{d}&lt;/b&gt;&quot;</span>, .{<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">self</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">computeTotals</span>()});\n    }\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">fn</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">send</span>(<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">self</span>: Report, buf: []<span class=\"hljs-type\">u8</span>) !void {\n        std.debug.<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;sending: {s}\\n&quot;</span>, .{<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">try</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">self</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">renderHtml</span>(buf)});\n    }\n};</code></pre><p><strong>✅ Idiomatic</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\"><code class=\"hljs language-zig\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">const</span> std = @<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">import</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;std&quot;</span>);\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">// Each concern is its own file in a real project: calc.zig,</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">// render.zig, deliver.zig: shown inline here as struct namespaces.</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">const</span> calc = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">fn</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">totals</span>(data: []<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">i32</span>) <span class=\"hljs-type\">i32</span> {\n        var sum: <span class=\"hljs-type\">i32</span> = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>;\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (data) |n| sum += n;\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> sum;\n    }\n};\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">const</span> render = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">fn</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">html</span>(buf: []<span class=\"hljs-type\">u8</span>, total: <span class=\"hljs-type\">i32</span>) ![]<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">u8</span> {\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> std.fmt.<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">bufPrint</span>(buf, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&lt;b&gt;{d}&lt;/b&gt;&quot;</span>, .{total});\n    }\n};\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">const</span> deliver = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">struct</span> {\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">fn</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">send</span>(html: []<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">u8</span>) void {\n        std.debug.<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;sending: {s}\\n&quot;</span>, .{html});\n    }\n};\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">pub</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">fn</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">main</span>() !void {\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">const</span> data = [_]<span class=\"hljs-type\">i32</span>{ <span class=\"hljs-number\">40</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">35</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">25</span> };\n    var buf: [<span class=\"hljs-number\">32</span>]<span class=\"hljs-type\">u8</span> = undefined;\n\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">const</span> total = calc.<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">totals</span>(&amp;data);\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">const</span> html = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">try</span> render.<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">html</span>(&amp;buf, total);\n    deliver.<span class=\"hljs-title function_ invoke__\">send</span>(html); <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// sending: &lt;b&gt;100&lt;/b&gt;</span>\n}</code></pre><p><strong>🧠 Note</strong>: In Zig every file <em>is</em> a struct, so &quot;one file, one concern&quot; is literally the\nmodule system: <code>@import(&quot;calc.zig&quot;)</code> and you&#39;re done. The split also narrows the fallible\npath: only rendering returns an error union, so <code>try</code> appears exactly where failure can\nhappen, and the caller owns the buffer instead of every concern touching it.</p>\n"}]},{"kind":"prose","id":"applications","title":"Applications","html":"<p>Where SRP shows up in practice:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Layered architecture</strong>: controller / service / repository each own one concern.</li>\n<li><strong>Reporting/exporting</strong>: compute, format, and deliver as separate units.</li>\n<li><strong>Auth</strong>: token issuing, verification, and storage split apart.</li>\n<li><strong>Logging</strong>: formatting vs transport vs level filtering.</li>\n</ul>\n"},{"kind":"prose","id":"related-principles-patterns","title":"Related Principles & Patterns","html":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Open/Closed</strong>: SRP-sized units are easier to extend without modification.</li>\n<li><strong>Facade</strong>: a coordinator that composes single-responsibility units behind one call.</li>\n<li><strong>Strategy / Decorator</strong>: each pulls one varying concern into its own object.</li>\n</ul>\n"}]}